<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58964" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοπ-ιάω</span></b> , fut. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άσω [ᾱ</span>]: aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκοπίᾱσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					<u>Phasm.</u>
					36
				</span></i>
			: pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεκοπίᾱκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Apoc.</u>
					2.3
				</span></i>
			: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόπος</span>):—<i>to be
				tired, grow weary</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				795
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				318.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>De.</u>
				25.18
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. τὰ σκέλη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
					147
				</span></i>
			, Men.l.c.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ὑπὸ ἀγαθῶν</span>
			<i>to be weary of</i> good things, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				735
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τῆς ὁδοιπορίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ev.Jo.</u>
					4.6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ διανοίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Erasistr.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>Consuet.</u>
				1
			</span></i>: c. part., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ὀρχούμενοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					602
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					12.46
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Asclep.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ κοπιάτω φιλοσοφῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					3p.59U.
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.185e
			</span></i>: aor.
			part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοπιάσας</span>, <i>defunctus laboribus,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				14.1811
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			 in act. sense, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				881a14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>work hard, toil,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ev.Matt.
				6.28
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεθ᾽ ἡδονῆς κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Vett.Val.
					266.6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴς τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>1 Ep.Ti.</u>
					4.10
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Rom.</u>
				16.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔν τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>1 Ep.Ti.</u>
					5.17
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Jo.</u>
					24.13
				</span></i>
			: c. inf., <i>strive, struggle</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ κοπία ζητεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Lyr.Alex.Adesp.</u>
					37.7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοπάζω</span>
			, <i>come to rest: arrive at a state of saturation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PLeid.X.
				30
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii/iv A. D.)</span>.</div>
